Think of a South African braai: a guest says, ‘I did not eat the last samosa—the dog stole it.’ Another guest asks, ‘Did you actually give the samosa to the dog?’ The first guest’s indignant answer would accidentally reveal that the excuse is false.

In the cartoon:
- the dog eating the homework is the excuse;
- the teacher’s question is the trap;
- Thandi’s indignant reply is the accidental confession;
- the virtual principal’s office provides the consequence.

Which teacher–Thandi exchange plays the role of the question that traps the guest at the braai?
